.TH HTTP_SENDREQ 3
.SH NAME
http_sendreq \- write the headers of a request
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B #include <http.h>
.P
.BI "int http_sendreq(http* " h ");"
.SH DESCRIPTION
.BR http_sendreq ()
puts the request line and the headers of the request that was started last into the output
buffer and flushes it, then calls
.BR http_body_flush (3)
for the body. This is done once; if the flush fails the headers are not queued again. After a
successful flush
.I h->sent
is set and the socket is watched for reading only (or also for writing if body data is left).
.P
It is called by
.BR http_canwrite (3)
and, with TLS, by
.BR http_canread (3).
.SH RETURN VALUE
0 on success, -1 on a write error, 0 also if there is no request.
.SH NOTES
The output buffer is flushed with buffer_flush(3), which does not keep what a non-blocking socket refuses. The headers are small enough to go out in one write.
.SH SEE ALSO
http_canwrite(3), http_body_flush(3)
